  "generated_by": "Hand-written expectations (G-392), written before any language ran. Each language's runner drives its real runtime offline with a fake model and asserts the outcome equals `expected`; `result` records those measured outcomes.",
  "pins_note": "Whether each approval decision reaches exactly the call it was issued for. Tools: `echo` (gated by mode, integer arg `n`) and `free` (ungated). The fake model's first reply is the row's `calls` in order; every later reply is the text `done`. Each round decides the listed approvals, by index into the parked step's pending approvals in issue order, as one batch where the language has one, then resumes once with an empty prompt; a decision the harness refuses is swallowed and the row continues. Recorded: `approvals` (how many approvals the first step issued), `free` (times the ungated tool ran) and `ran` (the sorted `n` of every echo that ran).",
